ew J. Stevenson | President, CEO & Director | Age 47 | Compensation: $1.4M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $436K ranks in the above the sector median among Consumer Cyclical peers. Each employee generates $24K of free cash flow annually. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (6/10).","financial_summary":["Holley Inc. is a micro-cap consumer cyclical business with a $255M market cap on $614M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -4% over the past three years, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 6% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, with gross margins sitting at 40%.","The business throws off $34M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 6 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 2.41\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 5.3\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 1.6\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 5.4% of the shares, and within its sector the business captures 1.6\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.3) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 54/100): leveraged balance sheet under pressure; durably derated by the market \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Revenue growth lags most Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Consumer Cyclical tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Consumer staples outperforming discretionary, signaling cautious spending","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 73% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Valued at a 32% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Contrasting Holley (NYSE:HLLY) and Denso (OTCMKTS:DNZOY)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/06/contrasting-holley-nysehlly-and-denso-otcmktsdnzoy.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793989732.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.869,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Holley (HLLY) Q3 2026 Earnings Call Transcript","source":"fool.com","link":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/11/05/holley-hlly-q3-2026-earnings-call-transcript/?sourc